{"id":"sudden-changes","title":"Billing that jumped, appeared from nowhere or stopped","tier":"REDFLAG","question":"Whose Medicaid billing changed too fast to be ordinary growth?","finding":"19 times a San Francisco biller at least tripled its Medicaid payments in one year to $500,000 or more; 5 provider numbers issued since 2018 took in $500,000 or more by the end of the following year; 3 billers taking $500,000 or more a year vanished from the file by 2022.","how":"Payments to each San Francisco billing number were added up by calendar year of service. Tripled: at least $50,000 the year before and three times that the next. New: the national registry shows the number was issued in 2018 or later and the first two calendar years reach $500,000. Stopped: $500,000 or more in its last year, and nothing after 2022.","limits":"Most of the steep climbs after 2021 have a plain cause: in January 2022 California added new Medi-Cal benefits (care management, medically tailored meals, housing help, community health workers), so new billers and fast growth were expected. An organization can also change its provider number, merge or be bought, which looks like a start or a stop, and 2020 was held down by the pandemic, so a 2021 rebound can look like a jump. 2024 is preliminary and small cells are withheld. The registry address is not the place of service.","columns":[{"k":"provider","t":"Provider","type":"org"},{"k":"npi","t":"Provider no.","type":"text"},{"k":"pattern","t":"What happened","type":"text"},{"k":"issued","t":"Number issued","type":"date"},{"k":"from","t":"From","type":"year"},{"k":"to","t":"To","type":"year"},{"k":"paidBefore","t":"Paid before","type":"usd"},{"k":"paidAfter","t":"Paid after","type":"usd"},{"k":"times","t":"Times","type":"times"},{"k":"service","t":"Main service","type":"text"}],"rows":[{"provider":"North Bay Aesthetics Inc A Professional Medical Corporation","npi":"1316645427","individual":false,"public":false,"pattern":"Large billing on a new prov